    "historical_decision": "Republic of Upper Volta and Burkina Faso are successive official names of one sovereign state. The U.S. Office of the Historian records U.S. recognition of Upper Volta on 5 August 1960 and states that the state's name changed from Upper Volta to Burkina Faso in 1984. Burkina Faso's Presidency records that on the first anniversary of the 4 August 1983 revolution, Sankara changed the country's name and Upper Volta became Burkina Faso. This is an official-name change, not state extinction/replacement.",
    "activity_rule": "Thomas Sankara's presidency is one continuous Activity from 4 August 1983 through 15 October 1987. The 4 August 1984 country-name change must not split the tenure.",
    "designation_rule": "Preserve Republic of Upper Volta / 오트볼타 공화국 as the temporal official_name of the continuous Burkina Faso polity from independence/recognition on 5 August 1960 through 3 August 1984, ending the day before the documented 4 August 1984 renaming."
